===Minotaur===
= died1
It's okay, we still have plenty of time — ironic, isn’t it? You’ve only just begun. Though losing to the Minotaur… you really outdid yourself.#speaker:Athena
Well, you know, when something’s angrily snorting right in your face, you kinda forget all about the cards.#speaker:Apistos
Next time, try growling back at him — who knows, maybe you’ll lose to something other than a card match.#speaker:Athena
I see you only wish the very best for me#speaker:Apistos
Sure thing, my little fish#speaker:Athena
If I didn't know, I’d never believe you were a goddess, your manners are atrocious, and your sense of humor… just as bad.#speaker:Apistos
Less words! Back to work!#speaker: Athena
->DONE
= died2
Let me guess—he was growling right in your face again, wasn’t he?#speaker:Athena
This time, even more aggressively...#speaker: Apistos
Yeah, yeah... That’s basically why you’re so out of steam lately.#speaker:Athena
So, you’re saying I’m just a poor, overworked guy to you?#speaker:Apistos
Poor? Nah, I think you’re pretty lucky to have me as your boss!#speaker: Athena
I’m seriously not so sure about that...#speaker: Apistos
Come on, my little fighter! Let’s go!#speaker: Athena
->DONE
=died3
You two had your little grudge match, and here you are again. Honestly, you’d be six feet under if it weren’t me. By the way, you and your bullheaded friend are starting to look like a real unlucky couple.#speaker:Athena
Being stuck with a huge, angry minotaur as a partner… yeah, that’s not exactly inspiring.#speaker:Apistos
Every creature deserves a partner, as you, mortals, say!#speaker:Athena
With that logic, I’d rather choose as a partner a really dumb salmon.#speaker:Apistos
Embracing your inner fishiness… how noble of you, Apistos!#speaker:Athena
Couldn’t be nobler…#speaker:Apistos
I promise, once you win the tournament, I’ll find you a salmon partner that suits you perfectly.#speaker:Athena
->DONE
